{
  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "The fix commit sha is fb4415d8aee6c1045be932a34fe6107c2f5ed147, authored by Jay Satiro on 2023-10-11, with subject 'socks: return error if hostname too long for remote resolve'.",
      "refs": ["fix", "commit:fb4415d8ae"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prior to the fix, when a SOCKS5 remote-resolve hostname exceeded 255 characters, the code attempted to silently fall back to local resolution by setting socks5_resolve_local = TRUE; this fallback did not work as intended and constituted the security issue (CVE-2023-38545).",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fix replaces the silent local-resolve fallback with an explicit hard error: it now calls failf() with a descriptive message and returns CURLPX_LONG_HOSTNAME, aborting the connection instead of continuing with a potentially unsafe state.",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae", "fix"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A secondary change in the same diff casts the hostname_len byte written into the SOCKS5 request buffer from (char) to (unsigned char), correcting a sign-extension issue for length values above 127.",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fix modifies exactly one source file (lib/socks.c) and adds one new regression test (tests/data/test728), also registering it in tests/data/Makefile.inc.",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The new test (test728) exercises the SOCKS5h path with an HTTP redirect to a 256-character hostname (one byte over the protocol limit) and verifies that curl returns error code 97 (CURLE_PROXY) with the exact error string 'SOCKS5: the destination hostname is too long to be resolved remotely by the proxy.'",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fix is a minimal, targeted change: no refactoring of surrounding logic, no new abstractions, and no changes to call sites outside the 255-character guard block in lib/socks.c.",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Residual risk — the fix only guards the remote-resolve code path (socks5_resolve_local == FALSE); the local-resolve path (socks5_resolve_local == TRUE from the outset) is not covered by the changed lines, though the 255-byte limit is only relevant when the proxy is asked to resolve. No evidence in the provided refs characterises any gap in the local-resolve path.",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Residual risk — the (unsigned char) cast fix for hostname_len is a correctness improvement but the diff contains no test that exercises a hostname between 128 and 255 bytes to confirm the cast is sufficient; coverage of that sub-range is not evidenced.",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The commit message references https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2023-38545.html as the associated bug report, linking the change to the CVE.",
      "refs": ["commit:fb4415d8ae", "fix"]
    }
  ],
  "confidence_notes": "All findings are grounded directly in the fix_commit diff and message (refs: fix, commit:fb4415d8ae). The provided evidence contains full diff text and commit metadata sufficient to characterise what changed and why. Evidence does not include: exploit reproduction steps, impact metrics, timeline of discovery/disclosure, or details of the broken fallback mechanism beyond the commit message description. Residual-risk assessments are derived from code absence in the diff, not from external sources. No other valid ref ids were usable because the diff fully describes the change on its own."
}
